cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kadı in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Kadı: Conformally Calibrated Decision Cascades in Front of Frontier Language Models"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: zencefilefendi
    name: "zencefil efendi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zencefilefendi/kadi"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - adaptive conformal inference
  - model cascades
  - LLM routing
  - knowledge distillation
  - uncertainty quantification
abstract: >-
  Kadı is a three-tier decision cascade (exact memory, local reflex, oracle LLM)
  whose local tier answers only when a split-conformal prediction set is a
  singleton, bounding the probability of disagreement with the oracle by a
  user-chosen alpha, marginally or per label. Calibration uses a random,
  held-out, continuously re-scored sample of the stream; Adaptive Conformal
  Inference and a statistically triggered drift breaker handle distribution shift.
